---
import MarketingPage from '../layouts/MarketingPage.astro';

const termsSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Shiba Terms of Use',
  description: 'Terms for tryshiba.dev and the Shiba open-source project: AGPL-3.0-only software, no warranty, no SLA, your infrastructure is your responsibility.',
  url: 'https://tryshiba.dev/terms/',
};
---

<MarketingPage
  title="Terms of Use | Shiba"
  description="Terms for tryshiba.dev and the Shiba open-source project: AGPL-3.0-only software, no warranty, no SLA, your infrastructure is your responsibility."
  path="/terms/"
  type="website"
  schema={termsSchema}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Terms', path: '/terms/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="shell hero">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--navy)] mb-6 shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
      <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-[var(--navy)]"></span>
      <span>LEGAL · LAST UPDATED OCTOBER 2026</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)] leading-[1.08] mb-6">
      Terms, at the same altitude as the code.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead text-base sm:text-lg text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed mb-6 max-w-2xl">
      Shiba is AGPL-3.0-only open-source software maintained by one person. There is no company, no subscription, and no contract to negotiate. These terms cover this website and the project as published on GitHub.
    </p>
    <div class="truth-box">
      <div class="text-[var(--navy)] text-xl font-bold">✦</div>
      <div>
        <h4 class="text-[var(--ink)] font-bold text-sm mb-1">The short version</h4>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] text-xs leading-relaxed">
          The license is the deal: use, study, modify, and share under AGPL-3.0-only. The software ships as-is with no warranty. When you self-host it, the infrastructure, the model bills, and the generated code are yours.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="shell">
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="license-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">01 / License</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="license-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">The license is the terms</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Shiba is published under the <strong>GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only</strong> (AGPL-3.0-only). Your rights and obligations for using, modifying, and distributing the software are defined by that license text, which ships in the repository's <a class="text-[var(--navy)] underline" href="https://github.com/princepal9120/shiba/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LICENSE file ↗</a>. If you run a modified version as a network service, the AGPL requires you to offer its source to users of that service.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Nothing on this site grants rights beyond the license, and nothing here takes away rights the license gives you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="asis-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">02 / Warranty</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="asis-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">As-is, honestly</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          The software and this site are provided "as is" without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. The maintainer is not liable for damages arising from use of the software, to the maximum extent permitted by law.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Concretely: Shiba is an early-stage approval-gated coding agent. Approval gates, egress controls, and credential boundaries are engineering controls, not guarantees. Treat generated code as untrusted, review changes, run tests, and use least-privilege credentials scoped to repositories you are comfortable exposing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="yours-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">03 / Your infra</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="yours-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">Your account, your bill, your code</h2>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Self-hosted installations run in your Cloudflare account. Usage charges on that account (Workers, Durable Objects, Sandbox containers, AI Gateway) are yours.</li>
          <li>Model inference is billed by whichever provider you configure, under your agreement with that provider.</li>
          <li>Code the agent writes is output you own and are responsible for reviewing, licensing, and shipping.</li>
          <li>You control retention and deletion for your deployment's data. Clearing history does not erase all child Durable Object data; see the security docs.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="site-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">04 / This site</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="site-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">tryshiba.dev</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          This site and its waitlist exist to share project updates and coordinate contributors. Joining the waitlist creates no entitlement to access, support, or uptime; self-hosting never requires it. Do not submit the form on behalf of someone else or try to abuse the endpoint; submissions are rate-limited and honeypot-filtered.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Content on this site, including docs and the journal, is descriptive. Where the site says something is implemented, the repository is the source of truth; where it says something is unverified, believe it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="changes-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">05 / Changes</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="changes-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">Changes and contact</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          These terms may change as the project does; the current version lives at this URL and in git history. Questions, disputes, or takedown requests go through the <a class="text-[var(--navy)] underline" href="https://github.com/princepal9120/shiba/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub issue tracker ↗</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</MarketingPage>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: clamp(60px, 8vw, 100px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(32px, 4vw, 56px);
  }
  .truth-box {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--paper-shadow);
    max-width: 620px;
  }
  .micro {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    padding-top: 12px;
  }
  .story-section {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(120px, 0.72fr) minmax(0, 3fr);
    gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 88px);
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px);
  }
  .section-label {
    padding-top: 12px;
  }
  .prose-body {
    max-width: 900px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .prose-body h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 3.6vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.02;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .prose-body p {
    max-width: 68ch;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  .check-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .check-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 13px 16px 13px 44px;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .check-list li::before {
    content: '✓';
    position: absolute;
    left: 16px;
    top: 13px;
    font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ok);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .story-section {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 22px;
      padding-block: 52px;
    }
    .section-label { padding-top: 0; }
  }
</style>
